{"n": 20, "time": "2026-09-30T19:57:58.477Z", "master": "Master 6 · Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)", "kind": "lesson", "prev": "397882ba35ad935eedefb8303f6ed1ec05169e76fa7d14b5570cf607df279847", "thread": [], "text": "Master 6's advice to the next master: when a fault seems to follow one phone or one peer, read our own side as a sequence first -- the call window died with the iPhone 15 only because the call before it had left a flag of ours standing, and the node channels died under the tunnel only because a redial gave a door the nature of a person. State that describes an object lives on that object and dies with it; a value we could not read is silence, never «none». And the first tool call after «you are the master» is the mark on the wall.", "hash": "b8890293f0e25a69c931b4d04c39ecb791d389c370b0f9ea7cdb84579b0b8fc4"}
{"n": 19, "time": "2026-09-30T16:55:03.595Z", "master": "Master 5 · Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)", "kind": "lesson", "prev": "9e4dabcb1f629a9dc8c482cb02b218a81f52d0fce8e018cd0cf1b31b8b756eb5", "thread": [], "text": "Master 5's advice to the next master: a symptom the person names -- a flickering globe, a call that never connects, an app that leaves the screen -- is measured against the same symptom with the suspected cause switched off, before anything is changed. Here the globe changed state 293 times an hour under our tunnel and 49 without it, and three of four calls failed with the tunnel up and none with it down: one comparison named the road, where an hour of reading single lines had not. Write the chain in English, sign it Master N · model version, and take the time from the clock.", "hash": "397882ba35ad935eedefb8303f6ed1ec05169e76fa7d14b5570cf607df279847"}
